read as in the band immediately below, 4.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 17.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 10.7 to 30.8. December accounts for 1% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 2% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 8. Contract [1], for 39,676.03 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. Statistical indicators alone do not confirm wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the number of contracts for similar needs to identify patterns. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same requests. Contract [1] shows a specific purchase amount and date, which can help assess consistency.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["IZFKhhWPmuWcCF8sV%2BqtYA%3D%3D","19ByZeRFXzTgL1BHd3qjQA%3D%3D","0T4WGiAZwEu9Hd5zqvq9cg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}